From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: TF_GLM_OVN_SIDE_PRIO, the prompt exchanges' side stream at the highest priority without a pair

A prompt chunk's pieced exchanges (partials, glue, shares) run on a side stream, cuda_forward_pieces.Pieces.side. Pieces.init
created it at the highest priority only for a pair (TF_GLM_PROMPT_PAIR, whose twin a server with solo passes does not hold);
every other server, the recipe's included (TF_GLM_CHUNK_SOLO=4096), ran it at the default priority, so its NCCL and glue
kernels were scheduled on equal terms with the main stream's grids. On the GB10 triangle the main stream sits idle about 11.7%
of a 4,096-row pass waiting for those exchanges.

TF_GLM_OVN_SIDE_PRIO=1 gives the stream the pair's priority without a pair: Pieces.high(pair) is `pair` or the switch, and
Pieces.init takes its result. Scheduling only: no kernel, buffer, event or order changes, so the bits are the same. Default
off: with the switch unset Pieces.high(pair) is `pair`, as before. The engine logs the priority at boot when the switch, not a
pair, set it. Production's own overlap stream has the same choice (TF_GLM_OVERLAP_PRIORITY, normal by default, with the note
that decode rounds after a high-priority prompt were about 0.5 to 1% slower), so decode is measured with it too.

Host test: the choice over pair and the switch (cuda_side_prio_test.zig, listed in cuda.zig's test block). The registry row
follows TF_GLM_OVN_LATENT_ROWS' and the docs line follows that switch's, so patches/pr1411's environment.zig and
docs/environment.md hunks still apply on top. Not run on a GPU yet.

New here, not a re-seat: written on this series at v1.2.9.

---

diff --git a/docs/environment.md b/docs/environment.md
index c552e368c55a69c91eb87179be7ad54e9df97c18..542305097e1bcd17a972986da8febcf88df9f591 100644
--- a/docs/environment.md
+++ b/docs/environment.md
@@ -104,6 +104,7 @@ Diagnostics quote and escape the supplied text so it cannot create another termi
 | `TF_GLM_OVN_ABSORB_VEC` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off (absorb_q and expand_v read bf16 kv_b by 16-byte loads) |
 | `TF_GLM_OVN_KVB8` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off (E4M3 kv_b read a 128-wide load times its scale) |
 | `TF_GLM_OVN_LATENT_ROWS` | `0`, `2` or `4`: the rows `absorb_q` and `expand_v` take in one loop step, with the same bits; default 0 (one row a step, today's kernels) |
+| `TF_GLM_OVN_SIDE_PRIO` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off (the prompt chunk's exchanges run on a side stream at the highest priority, ahead of the main stream's grids, as they do with `TF_GLM_PROMPT_PAIR`; the bits are the same) |
 | `TF_GLM_OVN_KDA_CHUNKED` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off (prompt chunks' KDA chain on production's chunked (WY) kernel; replies are not the serial chain's bit for bit) |
 | `TF_GLM_OVN_MM_WIDE` | Whole number; set, prompt linears take glm_mm's 128 x 128 blocks in L2 row bands (2: 32 x 32 warps, any other: 64 x 32); default 0 (off) |
 | `TF_GLM_OVN_MM_CLUSTER` | Whole count of Mi values; weights at least this large sum a decode tile's K slices in a cluster; default 0 (off) |
